{"name":"Lash growth serum (peptide)","deep":true,"image":null,"mentions":5,"casual":{"lead":["Lash serums are cosmetic liquids brushed along the upper lash line to make lashes look longer and fuller. Peptide versions are sold over the counter as an alternative to prescription prostaglandin products.","Brands say peptides condition and support lashes. The trial-level information in the sources covers bimatoprost (Latisse), whose manufacturer reports visible growth within 16 weeks and up to about 25 percent more length; no published human trials of peptide serums were found."],"sections":[{"h":"How people use it","paras":["People apply the serum along the base of the upper lashes, typically nightly, and keep using it for weeks while watching for changes. Some layer it with mascara or lash curling for added definition."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Risks & side effects","paras":["Peptide serums are sold as cosmetics and can cause irritation or allergy near the eye. For bimatoprost, reported effects include infection from reused applicators and eyelid darkening."],"subs":[]}]},"gallery":[{"url":"https://api.openverse.org/v1/images/adf1e15d-ec00-4a38-b495-10c1386b6eab/thumb/","full":"https://live.staticflickr.com/4513/26161521459_acb5989a4f_b.jpg","title":"Eye Wonder Lashes and Brows growth serum!","license":"BY 2.0","creator":"Unskinny Boppy","page":"https://www.flickr.com/photos/18509346@N00/26161521459","source":"Flickr"}],"links":{"studies":[{"title":"Nucleoside Analogues","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31644243/","source":"National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases, Bethesda (MD)","year":2012,"cites":0,"kind":"Review"},{"title":"Effect of glucagon-like peptide-1 receptor agonists and co-agonists on body composition: Systematic review and network meta-analysis.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/39719170/","source":"Metabolism: clinical and experimental","year":2025,"cites":null,"kind":"Network Meta-Analysis"},{"title":"Discontinuing glucagon