-peptide-taking.1786991/"},{"title":"can i hop on peptide while im in accutane phase 15 yo","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/can-i-hop-on-peptide-while-im-in-accutane-phase-15-yo.1785769/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20251228025826/https://looksmax.org/threads/can-i-hop-on-peptide-while-im-in-accutane-phase-15-yo.1785769/"},{"title":"best peptide for skin texture","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/best-peptide-for-skin-texture.1785255/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20251230190633/https://looksmax.org/threads/best-peptide-for-skin-texture.1785255/"}],"news":[],"social":[],"web":[{"title":"Eyelash — Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eyelash"},{"title":"Eyelash - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eyelash"},{"title":"Bimatoprost - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bimatoprost"}]},"angle":{"goal":"Eyes & eye area","chain":["Peptides applied to lash line","Lashes condition and may lengthen","Longer, fuller lashes"],"effect":"claimed","text":"Users apply over-the-counter peptide serums to the lash line for longer, fuller-looking lashes without a prescription. Brands say the peptides condition and support the lash. The prescription product bimatoprost has trial data; trials of the peptide versions were not found."},"wikipedia":{"title":"Eyelash","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eyelash"},"grokipedia":null,"lead":["Peptide lash growth serums are over-the-counter cosmetic products applied to the lash line to make lashes look longer or fuller. Some brands use peptides instead of prostaglandin analogues, and a reference work links this to regulatory rules in Canada and California.[1]","The best-documented lash-growth product is bimatoprost (Latisse), a prescription prostaglandin analogue; its manufacturer reports visible growth within 16 weeks and up to about 25 percent more length.[1][2] The sources reviewed contain no published human trials of peptide serums."],"infobox":[["Type","Cosmetic serum"],["Route","Topical, at the lash line"],["Active ingredients","Peptides (varies by brand)"],["Comparator","Bimatoprost (Latisse), the approved product"],["Legal status","Cosmetic (OTC)"]],"sections":[{"h":"Background","paras":["Lash length is largely genetic, with upper lashes typically about 3 to 10 mm (usually 7 to 8 mm), and follicle number is set before birth.[1] Growth conditioners and serums, often built on seed extracts, minerals and other chemicals, have become common over the past decade.[1] Latisse, approved in 2009, was the first drug to receive FDA approval for eyelash growth.[1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Prostaglandin versus peptide products","paras":["Bimatoprost is a prostaglandin F2-alpha analogue originally approved for glaucoma in 2001; its lash use is a cosmetic indication.[2] Its reported adverse effects with cosmetic use include infection if single-use applicators are reused and darkening of the eyelid skin.[2] Some cosmetic serums avoid prostaglandins and use peptides instead.[1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found on peptide lash serums. The reviewed sources describe studies only of bimatoprost."],"subs":[]}],"lore":{"intro":"On looksmax.org, users ask which lash serum to use and compare options such as Latisse, a water-based serum from The Ordinary, castor oil and rosemary oil.","claims":[{"claim":"Latisse is the lash serum to use for thicker lashes","verdict":"unknown","note":""},{"claim":"Topical minoxidil can be combined with a lash serum for faster results","verdict":"unknown","note":""},{"claim":"A water-based peptide serum works as well as an oil","verdict":"unknown","note":""}]},"timeline":[{"year":"2001","event":"Bimatoprost approved in the US for glaucoma.[2]"},{"year":"2009","event":"Latisse becomes the first FDA-approved product for eyelash growth.[1]"}],"refs":[{"title":"Eyelash","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eyelash","source":"Wikipedia","year":2025,"type":"encyclopedia"},{"title":"Bimatoprost","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bimatoprost","source":"Wikipedia","year":2025,"type":"encyclopedia"}],"studies":[],"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"Peptide and \"supplement\" stack to get to 6'4 13%bf (high IQ)","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/peptide-and-supplement-stack-to-get-to-64-13-bf-high-iq.1791239/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260102080448/https://looksmax.org/threads/peptide-and-supplement-stack-to-get-to-64-13-bf-high-iq.1791239/"},{"title":"Peptide Suggestions For Me","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/peptide-suggestions-for-me.1790948/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20251229104522/https://looksmax.org/threads/peptide-suggestions-for-me.1790948/"},{"title":"peptide help pls","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/peptide-help-pls.1789685/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20251228112153/https://looksmax.org/threads/peptide-help-pls.1789685/"},{"title":"peptide vendor p2","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/peptide-vendor-p2.1788940/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20251228031000/https://looksmax.org/threads/peptide-vendor-p2.1788940/"},{"title":"peptide research questions","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/peptide-research-questions.1788241/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260302142810/https://looksmax.org/threads/peptide-research-questions.1788241/"},{"title":"peptide sources","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/peptide-sources.1780858/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260307202149/https://looksmax.org/threads/peptide-sources.1780858/"},{"title":"peptide stack recommendatiosn please please","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/peptide-stack-recommendatiosn-please-please.1780311/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260311103328/https://looksmax.org/threads/peptide-stack-recommendatiosn-please-please